{#-
  The index of every world, written once and shown after <main> on every page but the two that
  list every page themselves (sitemap.html, moods.html). It is the one list of worlds the site
  has, and _data/worlds.json is the one place the list and every world's name are kept: a world
  is added, renamed or retired there, and this include, the header, sitemap.html and the sky
  circuit all follow.

  Two groups, in the words every page uses: off the sky (worlds that share nothing but the site)
  and under the sky (worlds that read one saved sky). Under each name is the orientation the world
  answers to, which is the same phrase the ribbon reads a visitor as. On a world under the sky that
  group comes first and says where in that circuit this world is.

  One shared suggestion of where to go next lives in this include: a single circuit link at the
  bottom of the panel. It is always one world name as a plain link, and it advances through the
  same off-sky then under-sky order for everyone.

  The headings are real (h2, then h3), so a visitor listening to the page hears its shape, and the
  reachability axiom holds with scripting off because every link here is plain markup.
-#}
{%- set here = (page.filePathStem | replace('/', '')) + '.html' if page else '' -%}
{%- set skyIndex = -1 -%}
{%- for world in worlds.underSky %}{% if world.file == here %}{% set skyIndex = loop.index0 %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- set skyCount = worlds.underSky.length -%}
{%- set groups = [['sky', 'under the sky', worlds.underSky], ['off', 'off the sky', worlds.offSky]] if skyIndex >= 0 else [['off', 'off the sky', worlds.offSky], ['sky', 'under the sky', worlds.underSky]] -%}
{%- set circuit = worlds.offSky.concat(worlds.underSky) -%}
{%- set circuitIndex = -1 -%}
{%- for world in circuit %}{% if world.file == here %}{% set circuitIndex = loop.index0 %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- set nextWorld = circuit[(circuitIndex + 1) % circuit.length] if circuit.length else null -%}
<footer class='site-footer'>
  <nav class='panel worlds' aria-labelledby='worlds-title'>
    <h2 class='panel-title' id='worlds-title'>every world</h2>
    <p class='panel-note'>{{ (worlds.offSky.length + skyCount) | words | capitalize }} worlds and no default. Under each name is who the site would send there: take the one that fits, or the one that does not.</p>
    <div class='worlds-groups'>
{%- for group in groups %}
      <section class='worlds-group' aria-labelledby='worlds-{{ group[0] }}'>
        <h3 class='panel-label' id='worlds-{{ group[0] }}'>{{ group[1] }}</h3>
{%- if group[0] == 'sky' %}
{%- if skyIndex >= 0 %}
        <p class='panel-note'>These {{ skyCount | words }} read one saved sky, the stars placed in the wish constellation. This is {{ skyIndex + 1 }} of {{ skyCount }} in that sky circuit.</p>
{%- else %}
        <p class='panel-note'>These {{ skyCount | words }} read one saved sky; the wish constellation is where it is placed.</p>
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
        <ul class='chips chips-tall'>
{%- for world in group[2] %}
          <li><a href='{{ siteRoot }}{{ world.file }}'{% if world.file == here %} class='current' aria-current='page'{% endif %}>{{ world.name }}<span>{{ world.orientation }}</span></a></li>
{%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </section>
{%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class='panel-foot'>
{%- if nextWorld %}
      <a class='action' href='{{ siteRoot }}{{ nextWorld.file }}'>{{ nextWorld.name }}</a>
{%- endif %}
      <span><a href='{{ siteRoot }}sitemap.html'>site map</a></span>
    </p>
  </nav>
</footer>